From: validol1979-ops <225744605+validol1979-ops@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 11:33:58 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 06/10] offload: BackendDram writes every slice (host row
 mailboxes at S > 1)

BackendDram wrote slice 0 only, so the row servers (Gemma 4's PLE rows, Qwen's embed_host) fed one
slice while every slice runs the same program and reads its own DRAM. Without an explicit slice it now
broadcasts writes to all cfg.S slices (reads stay on slice 0); an explicit s keeps the old behaviour.
IsaBackend exposes cfg. tests/test_offload_server.py: PLE / Qwen mailbox with fake and ISA backends at
S = 1 / 2. tests/test_offload*.py: 117 passed, 1 failed (test_pool_file_counts_its_reads_by_the_page_cache,
fails on the unpatched tree too: page-cache environment). Codex gpt-6.1-sol (medium), reviewed.

diff --git a/opentpu/host/offload.py b/opentpu/host/offload.py
index a68f2202..fbfffd4f 100644
--- a/opentpu/host/offload.py
+++ b/opentpu/host/offload.py
@@ -1689,14 +1689,20 @@ class SimDram:
 
 class BackendDram:
     """A backend's DRAM (write(s, addr, array) / read(s, addr, n): IsaBackend, RtlBackend,
-    BoardBackend) as ExpertServer's memory; one slice (the board's)."""
+    BoardBackend) as server memory. By default writes broadcast to every slice and reads
+    use slice 0: all slices run the same row requests and need the rows and served word in
+    their own DRAM. An explicit s selects one slice for both reads and writes."""
 
-    def __init__(self, backend, s: int = 0):
-        self.backend, self.s = backend, s
+    def __init__(self, backend, s: int | None = None):
+        self.backend, self.s = backend, 0 if s is None else s
+        self.slices = (range(getattr(getattr(backend, "cfg", None), "S", 1))
+                       if s is None else (s,))
 
     def write(self, addr: int, data) -> None:
         b = data if isinstance(data, np.ndarray) else np.frombuffer(bytes(data), np.uint8)
-        self.backend.write(self.s, addr, np.ascontiguousarray(b).view(np.uint8).reshape(-1))
+        b = np.ascontiguousarray(b).view(np.uint8).reshape(-1)
+        for s in self.slices:
+            self.backend.write(s, addr, b)
 
     def read(self, addr: int, n: int) -> bytes:
         return np.asarray(self.backend.read(self.s, addr, n)).view(np.uint8).tobytes()
